NEARS-1574 AC9 — loading branch (branch 1, hasOpenStoreNearby == null) recapture.

WHY THE FIRST SHOT WAS WRONG
The original ac9-loading-skeleton.png was DELETED. Its a11y measurement and its
screencap were two separate adb round-trips, so the frame published was the
CONTENT branch with flash-sale images still fetching (populated chip row + a real
store tile reading "0.37 KM FROM YOU"), not the loading branch.

INSTRUMENT THAT ACTUALLY WORKS
Emulator-console `network delay/speed` shapes the emulated RADIO; the app reaches
the host at 10.0.2.2 over a route that shaping does not slow, so the branch-1
window stayed shorter than one uiautomator dump cycle (~1-2s) even at
`delay gprs / speed gsm`. What works:
  1. Let the app fully load the MODULE SELECTOR first (module data cached).
  2. `kill -STOP <backend pid holding :8010>`  -> the store fetch hangs.
  3. Tap into Food & Restaurant. storeModel stays null -> branch 1 holds open.
  4. `kill -CONT` afterwards.
(Suspending the backend BEFORE a cold start does not work: it stalls the module
gate before the Food home ever mounts.)

PROOF THE FRAME IS INSIDE THE WINDOW (sandwich capture)
a11y dumped immediately BEFORE and immediately AFTER the screencap; the frame is
kept only if BOTH satisfy the branch-1 signature. Both dumps came back
byte-identical: xml_sha=3711a84f5d, 16 labelled nodes.

